From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:27:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t604x-j614-j616: scale the 720p camera
 preset

The 1280x720 preset cropped the top-left 1280x720 corner of the 1920x1080
window that firmware configuration 5 delivers, without scaling. A 720p
stream, which video calls often ask for, therefore showed an off-centre
view about two thirds as wide as the 1080p one.

Crop the whole 1920x1080 window and let the scaler bring it down to
1280x720, as the driver already does for the sizes it derives itself
(such as 640x480 from the 1080p crop).

The driver offered P010 only for presets whose crop equals their output,
so the scaled preset would lose it and a 1280x720 P010 request would fall
back to 1280x960. Accept a crop at the origin with the output's aspect
ratio that is no smaller than the output instead.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(backported from commit 99ec97ea334b71a055e1c9fb2f48b46096c11f22)
[j604: the t604x-j614-j616.dtsi hunk is dropped: this tree has no J614/J616 camera DT. The driver hunk is taken for the J604's scaled 720p preset.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
index 1881d22482..15b1ca2816 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
@@ -329,8 +329,10 @@ static int isp_ch_cache_sensor_configs(struct apple_isp *isp, u32 ch, u32 count)
 			    preset->input_dim.x == config->in_width &&
 			    preset->input_dim.y == config->in_height &&
 			    !preset->crop_offset.x && !preset->crop_offset.y &&
-			    preset->crop_size.x == preset->output_dim.x &&
-			    preset->crop_size.y == preset->output_dim.y)
+			    /* Same aspect ratio, never enlarged: the scaler may shrink it. */
+			    preset->crop_size.x >= preset->output_dim.x &&
+			    preset->crop_size.x * preset->output_dim.y ==
+			    preset->crop_size.y * preset->output_dim.x)
 				preset->p010 = preview || reported;
 		}
 		if (!cached->usable)
